Speaker 2: Trump's personal lawyer, Rudy Giuliani, was just hit with a $148 million judgment for cruelty and defamation that he inflicted against them.

755
00:59:59,720 --> 01:00:03,900
Speaker 2: Other state and local elected officials across the country faced similar personal attacks.

756
01:00:04,861 --> 01:00:10,271
Speaker 2: In addition, Fox News agreed to pay a record 8 -- $787 million for the lies they told about voter fraud.

757
01:00:17,240 --> 01:00:19,575
Speaker 2: Let's be clear about the 2020 election.

758
01:00:21,540 --> 01:00:25,956
Speaker 2: Trump exhausted every legal avenue available to him to overturn the election.

759
01:00:26,518 --> 01:00:26,940
Speaker 2: Every one.

760
01:00:28,220 --> 01:00:36,120
Speaker 2: But the legal path just took Trump back to the truth that I had won the election and he was a loser.

761
01:00:42,500 --> 01:00:54,470
Speaker 2: Well, for knowing how his mind works now, he had one -- he had one act left, one desperate act available to him.

762
01:00:55,613 --> 01:00:58,584
Speaker 2: The violence of January the 6th.

763
01:01:00,250 --> 01:01:05,990
Speaker 2: And since that day, more than 1,200 people have been charged for their soul in the Capitol.

764
01:01:06,693 --> 01:01:09,630
Speaker 2: Nearly 900 of them have been convicted or pled guilty.

765
01:01:10,430 --> 01:01:14,605
Speaker 2: Collectively to date, they have been sentenced to more than 840 years in prison.

766
01:01:23,392 --> 01:01:24,294
Speaker 2: What's Trump done?

767
01:01:25,557 --> 01:01:31,470
Speaker 2: Instead of calling them criminals, he's called these insurrectionists patriots.

768
01:01:32,290 --> 01:01:32,953
Speaker 2: They're patriots.

769
01:01:33,856 --> 01:01:37,110
Speaker 2: And he promised to pardon them if he returns to office.

770
01:01:37,930 --> 01:01:40,987
Speaker 2: Trump said that there was a lot of love on January the 6th.

